{"id": "EUVD-2026-80631", "enisaUuid": "723fc59a-18e7-3899-a9d4-dbe63bffa010", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_mass_storage: fix null pointer dereference in fsg_common_set_num_buffers()\n\nPreviously fsg_num_buffers_validate() was removed as it was not\nnecessary due to Kconfig setting the limits for n from 2 to 256 with\ndefault as 2. However, setting the page content in such a way that\nkstrtou8() reflects n value as either 0 or 1 bypasses these\nrestrictions leading to a null pointer dereference if n is 0. Fix\nthis by adding a check for n < 2 and returning -EINVAL if n is\neither 0 or 1 consistent with Kconfig logic.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4f0fe3ab47ed57ee4974fdd3e9dccb7839a7ebf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51cc9af4f2d3f0b765266aced66b9b532b423b13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e8dd2a7a8ccbb756771ad985b0ad3387ed3c957", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9b5b5df5b8dd3c1572ed267200276a44cc67d8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c0f5ca48674a5b5f9fa4a9c3325aa48053af0bc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90023", "GHSA-4pqp-h39m-gcw4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "141686b2-66cd-3b41-9f6c-6c24f4d63049", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe5a6c48fd954489f51aab151d5dad9254c76419 <f4f0fe3ab47ed57ee4974fdd3e9dccb7839a7ebf"}, {"id": "257a7e6f-8c90-3df2-84b8-cde9471f2901", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fe5a6c48fd954489f51aab151d5dad9254c76419 <b9b5b5df5b8dd3c1572ed267200276a44cc67d8e"}, {"id": "49cd66e5-2657-359a-a38f-ec685212ba2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "4c0372bf-0ee0-3d2d-9da4-1ee320f1e0a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, 